## One architectural point we should make explicit

We should **not necessarily persist Machine 1 and Machine 2 as two database columns**.

The conceptual model is two state machines.

The implementation question is:

> What is the minimum existing/new persistence representation needed to faithfully implement Machine 2 while leaving Machine 1 untouched?

That's what Claude should determine before coding.

So I would now consider the **architecture itself frozen for the next TDD planning step**:

```text
                 Election Membership
                         │
              ┌──────────┴──────────┐
              │                     │
              ▼                     ▼
       MACHINE 2                MACHINE 1
   Election Membership       Voting Engine
        Lifecycle              Allowance
              │                     │
   INVITED / ACTIVE /         ACTIVE / INACTIVE
   SUSPENDED / REMOVED
              │                     │
              └──────────┬──────────┘
                         │
             Cross-machine invariant:
             only Machine-2 ACTIVE
             may have Machine-1 ACTIVE
                         │
                         ▼
                  Voting Engine
```

**Yes — this is the direction I would proceed with.** The next Claude task should therefore be **TDD implementation planning against this frozen architecture**, not another conceptual redesign.
